 "summary": "President Clinton's first home in Hope, Arkansas, in real LEGO parts, at a larger size: a 1917 American Foursquare in white clapboard with dark green corner boards and window frames, under a tall pale green hipped roof with wide white eaves and a dormer over the front. The full-width front porch stands on four square white columns, with the front door under its transom, a hanging porch light and two black rocking chairs. A low black iron fence runs along the sidewalk, with a back door on its stoop and two tall shade trees behind. Inside, the late 1940s: the grandfather in the parlor by the floor radio, the mother on the living room sofa with the little boy at his blocks on the rug, the dining table laid for six, and the grandmother at the kitchen stove; upstairs, the grandparents' room, the mother's room, the nursery with its crib and toy train, a sewing room and a tiled bathroom with a claw-foot tub.",
